The hero section revolves entirely around the koi fish.

The koi is NOT:
- a decorative asset
- a floating background object
- a looping idle model
- a “3D element”

The koi is the soul of the experience.

It should feel:
- alive
- intelligent
- graceful
- cinematic
- mysterious
- physically present
- emotionally atmospheric

The fish must command visual attention naturally WITHOUT screaming for attention.

====================================================
CORE HERO PHILOSOPHY
====================================================

The first thing users should feel is:

“There’s something alive in this environment.”

The koi should emerge slowly from darkness/fog/light rays rather than instantly appearing fully visible.

The hero experience should feel like:
- discovering a mythical cybernetic ocean creature
- underwater cinematic encounter
- high-end interactive digital art piece

====================================================
TECHNICAL STACK
====================================================

Use:
- React Three Fiber
- Drei
- GSAP
- Framer Motion
- Three.js
- GLSL shaders where necessary

DO NOT use:
- primitive keyframe animations only
- robotic rotation loops
- constant circular motion
- generic floating animation presets

====================================================
HERO COMPOSITION
====================================================

The koi must remain the dominant focal point of the hero section.

Composition rules:
- fish positioned slightly off-center
- cinematic asymmetry
- large negative space around fish
- fish occupies depth space, not flat screen space
- environment frames the koi

The camera should compose the koi like a film shot.

The fish should occasionally:
- drift closer to camera
- pass partially outside frame
- rotate elegantly
- disappear partially into volumetric fog

Avoid keeping the fish perfectly centered permanently.

====================================================
MOVEMENT SYSTEM
====================================================

This is the MOST IMPORTANT part.

The movement MUST feel biologically believable.

The koi should swim with:
- inertia
- drag
- acceleration
- deceleration
- curved motion paths
- subtle unpredictability

The motion should NEVER:
- loop obviously
- repeat visibly
- feel mathematically robotic

====================================================
BODY ANIMATION
====================================================

Animate the entire body chain.

The fish motion should propagate:
head → spine → tail

Implement:
- sine-wave spine deformation
- delayed tail follow-through
- soft secondary motion
- subtle fin movement
- slight body twisting

The tail should lag behind directional changes naturally.

Movement references:
- real koi swimming underwater
- slow cinematic underwater footage
- graceful whale-like drifting

====================================================
SWIMMING LOGIC
====================================================

Create procedural roaming behavior.

The fish should:
- wander naturally
- choose new paths occasionally
- arc around invisible points
- react subtly to cursor proximity
- avoid sudden directional snaps

The fish should:
- sometimes slow almost to stillness
- sometimes accelerate gently
- sometimes glide through the camera frame

DO NOT:
- make it constantly active
- make it hyper energetic

The motion pacing should feel meditative.

====================================================
CURSOR INTERACTION
====================================================

Cursor interaction must be subtle and premium.

The koi should:
- slightly acknowledge cursor presence
- gently rotate toward cursor
- shift trajectory softly
- never aggressively chase the cursor

Think:
curiosity, not game AI.

The response should be:
- dampened
- delayed
- elegant

====================================================
SCROLL INTERACTION
====================================================

The fish should react to scroll progression.

Examples:
- camera slowly follows fish
- fish dives deeper while scrolling
- fish ascends through fog
- fish passes through light shafts
- fish approaches text reveals

The fish must feel connected to page progression.

====================================================
ENTRANCE SEQUENCE
====================================================

On initial load:

DO NOT instantly reveal the fish.

Instead:
1. dark underwater atmosphere
2. faint particles
3. subtle god rays
4. distant silhouette
5. slow emergence
6. emissive highlights reveal scales gradually

The reveal should feel cinematic.

====================================================
SHADER & MATERIAL QUALITY
====================================================

The koi material MUST feel premium.

Implement:
- reflective wet surface
- subtle emissive accents
- soft iridescence
- realistic specular response
- subtle translucency in fins

Possible enhancements:
- fresnel rim lighting
- animated caustic projections
- soft bloom highlights
- depth-based lighting

Avoid:
- plastic appearance
- flat PBR defaults
- over-glowing neon fish
- cartoon rendering

====================================================
LIGHTING
====================================================

Lighting should sculpt the koi dramatically.

Use:
- soft rim lighting
- underwater caustics
- moving light rays
- subtle bloom
- volumetric-inspired depth

The koi should periodically pass through:
- brighter shafts of light
- darker fog regions
- silhouette moments

This creates cinematic rhythm.

====================================================
CAMERA CHOREOGRAPHY
====================================================

The camera should NOT remain static.

Use:
- subtle drift
- slow buoyant movement
- eased interpolation
- underwater float sensation

The camera should:
- frame the fish artistically
- move with cinematic restraint
- never spin wildly

The fish and camera should feel connected.

====================================================
PARTICLES & ENVIRONMENT
====================================================

Around the koi include:
- floating particles
- suspended dust
- tiny drifting bubbles
- volumetric fog layers
- soft depth haze

Particles should react subtly to fish movement.

The koi should feel embedded in water, not floating in empty space.

====================================================
ATMOSPHERE
====================================================

The emotional tone should be:
- calm
- mysterious
- immersive
- majestic
- slightly haunting

NOT:
- playful
- cartoonish
- gaming-style flashy
- overly cyberpunk

====================================================
PERFORMANCE REQUIREMENTS
====================================================

Optimize carefully.

Use:
- adaptive DPR
- optimized render loops
- efficient animation calculations
- instanced particles
- compressed textures

Maintain smooth FPS.

Avoid:
- excessive postprocessing
- expensive real-time shadows everywhere
- overkill shader complexity

====================================================
IMPORTANT ANTI-SLOP RULES
====================================================

DO NOT produce:
- generic “floating object” animation
- copy-pasted R3F examples
- default Drei orbit feeling
- fake cinematic effects
- exaggerated bloom spam
- oversaturated neon visuals
- robotic loops

Everything must feel:
intentional, restrained, elegant, cinematic.

====================================================
FINAL GOAL
====================================================

Users should immediately feel:

“This fish feels alive.”

The koi should become:
- the identity of the website
- the emotional anchor
- the cinematic centerpiece
- the memory users retain after leaving

The final hero should feel closer to:
interactive underwater cinema

than:
a normal React website with a fish model.
